# Cloudflare Workers static-asset redirects. Parsed by Workers out of the
# deployed asset directory (Vite copies public/ into dist/, the same way it
# carries _headers), evaluated top-down, first match wins.
#
# Phase 6 Task 1 (#65, P6.1). T-02 fixes the candidate URL at
# /<workspace-slug>/<test-slug>, which is a path with no file behind it, so
# without a rule here the asset router answers every candidate link with
# dist/404.html before the page ever loads. The rule is a 200 rewrite, not a
# redirect: the address bar must keep the slug pair, because src/exam-main.tsx
# reads it to know which test to ask the API about.
#
# ORDERING IS THE WHOLE OF IT. /:workspaceSlug/:testSlug matches any
# two-segment path, which includes /assets/index-abc123.js and
# /fonts/anek-latin.woff2 — so those two are claimed first, as explicit
# pass-throughs, and the fallback is last. Nothing may be added below it.
#
# /api/* and /t/* need no rule: wrangler.toml's run_worker_first sends both
# to the Worker, and redirects here are not applied to a request the Worker
# serves. /index.html, /admin.html, /exam.html and /404.html are single
# segment, which the fallback's two-segment pattern cannot match.

/assets/*  /assets/:splat  200
/fonts/*   /fonts/:splat   200

/:workspaceSlug/:testSlug  /exam.html  200
